YAAP-scorchgeek-Ran-Elf-Mal-Cha

This was my second ascension; my first I never posted about, which was
a wizard. I have recently had five Valkyries die in late game, so I
decided to try some other roles.

This game went very smoothly, nothing in particular really happened.
The one thing that surprised me was how little I used my bow. After I
did the quest, I got crowned and used Stormbringer for the rest of the
game, and although I did enchant a stack of arrows to +3 and poison
them, I rarely used them. In the late game, I used loads of c corpses
as well.

The early game went quite nicely. I found no lamps in Minetown, but
found both a magic lamp and an oil lamp sitting around in the lower
levels of the Mines. I kept the lamp around for the light source for
quite a while. There were surprisingly few close escapes in the early
game, maybe partly because I kept using ranged weapons (surprise!). I
also built up a stack of daggers in the Mines and used those most of
the time to save my arrows. The Minetown altar was also coaligned, and
I came back to sacrifice a bit once I found two bags of tricks in the
lower levels of the Mines. I also found mithril, and, with my starting
elven cloak, I had a nice AC to continue down the dungeon.

By this time I had found no less than four artifacts: I found two
worthless artifacts on the order of Trollsbane in the early levels of
the main dungeon, Vorpal Blade in a Minetown general store ("For you,
my lady, only 21662 for this Vorpal Blade"), and was gifted Sting
(whoops!) later. Shortly after I left the Mines, I found Excalibur in
a bones pile. I never used or took any of these along, although I
could have stopped in Minetown for a few of them on my way up if I was
interested in increasing my score. I also named Orcrist and sacrificed
a bit more in the hopes of Stormbringer, but didn't get anything else
before my create monster ran out. I ditched my daggers for arrows
since my luck had been increased and left.

At level ten I hit a bigroom, which I cleared out fairly easily with
my Sting and 5-arrow multishot. However, on the same bigroom, I hit a
poly trap, which turned me into a useless monster and destroyed my
nice mithril and +2 elven cloak. Annoyed, I rubbed my magic lamp and
wished for +3 GDSM (had "oR sokoban), which I thankfully got.
Unfortunately, all the way down to level 18, I found no more cloaks. I
even went as far as killing a few peaceful elves, but nothing but
elven leather helms resulted. This led to a couple of level drains by
wraiths. I found a sink, got a succubus, and boosted my level to 18,
then attempted the quest. I found it quite easy, despite the fast
centaurs, and Scorpius was a joke.

I left and stashed some of my stuff away by the portal, since I didn't
get a bag of holding until I wished for one at the Castle. Then I went
on. Halfway down to the castle, I noticed that an annoying number of
my arrows were breaking, so I zapped my wand of enlightenment, and
noticed that not only was my luck status only "lucky", I had
accidentally left my luckstone behind. Aargh! So I went back to
Minetown, sacrificed some more, and found my luckstone back at my
stash.

When I finally reached the castle, it took me forever to clear it out
because I didn't have an instrument and had to smash the drawbridge. I
had to resort to using a 58% fail magic missile spell because I was
running out of arrows, even with the Longbow of Diana (which worked
surprisingly well). The wand of wishing was 0:1.

Oddly enough, there were no other altars in the entire dungeon besides
Minetown, so I went back, maxed out my luck, and got crowned for
Stormbringer. At this point, though, I accidentally attacked the high
priest, so I left. I later came back with charm monster and sacrificed
some more, only to hit the priest with Stormy yet again, and I had
forgotten charm monster.

I had to go back to Minetown and the Castle about four times, because
I kept forgetting things: my sack with lots of stuff (which, after I
wasted a cursed teleport and 2500 turns of walking back, turned out to
be in my bag of holding which was with me all along), a pickaxe to dig
through Gehennom, a forgotten spell, etc. This was perhaps the most
annoying section of the game.

Gehennom went by quickly, thanks to me learning magic mapping from a
randomly generated spellbook. Not only did I find a rubber chicken in
Orcus-town and get the wand of death with no charges wasted, I also
found a wand of wishing sitting on the floor.

I levelported into the Sanctum, skipped the graveyard, wished for 3
cursed potions of gain level, and got out in less than five minutes.
The mysterious force was pretty fair, in terms of the number of times
it hit me. I had an extra wand of wishing and fully charged magic
marker, so I wrote a couple of scrolls of charging, gold detection,
and genocide for the Plane of Water, and breezed through the endgame.
I wished for a chickatrice corpse on Astral, killed the angels that
had been sent after me for having conflict, and the first altar was
mine.


